# Content transformers

- Resolve normal wikilinks without touching the same text inside `![[embeds]]`. Missing wikilinks become disabled markup and never add graph edges.
- Parse inline tags from Markdown text nodes after protecting code and comments. Record tags on the processed file so the index can merge them with frontmatter tags after publication filtering.
- A callout title needs a blank blockquote line before its body. Otherwise Markdown merges them into one paragraph.
- Rehype Pretty Code may put `data-language` on `pre` or `code`; the code-block slot must read both.
- Mermaid fences become inert diagram markup through the OFM remark contribution. The browser renderer is a lazy, route-owned resource with strict Mermaid security. Keep diagram source inside protected payloads for encrypted notes.
- Resolve first-party browser resource import IDs from the Vite package, since a consumer app does not need a direct `@svartz/plugins` dependency.
